.TH git-parhel 1  "parhel 0.2.2" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git\-parhel \- Create Git worktrees with copy\-on\-write, so node_modules, target/ and other ignored build output come along without using extra disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit parhel\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
git parhel creates regular Git worktrees by cloning the source worktree with the filesystem\*(Aqs copy\-on\-write support instead of checking files out. Ignored directories such as node_modules/ and target/ come along and share disk blocks with the source until one side changes them.
.PP
The result is an ordinary worktree: list, move, lock and remove it with `git worktree`.
.PP
Platform support: macOS on APFS (clonefile). Linux and Windows are planned. Elsewhere, `add \-\-fallback` creates a regular worktree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
git\-parhel\-add(1)
Create a copy\-on\-write worktree
.TP
git\-parhel\-doctor(1)
Diagnose the environment and clean up after crashed runs
.TP
git\-parhel\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  git parhel add ../my\-feature \-\-new\-branch feature/my\-feature
  git parhel add ../hotfix \-\-branch release/1.2
  git parhel add ../review \-\-detach v1.4.0
  git parhel doctor \-\-fix

Remove a worktree with `git worktree remove <path>`.
Docs: https://github.com/myrk\-kale/parhel
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
